{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Silly Superstitions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Careful With the Mirror", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> when you want to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> to talk about situations in the past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + to be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">  You <span class=\"strong\">are supposed to</span> throw salt over your shoulder. <br/>I <span class=\"strong\">am supposed to</span> spin around three times. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say be supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Romans who believed that life was supposed to renew again every seven years. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you break a mirror you are supposed to throw salt over your shoulder. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are supposed to immediately spin around three times.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use an active structure when you want the \"doer\" of the action to be the subject. <br/>You use a passive structure when you want the \"receiver\" of the action to be the subject. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Active sentence = The Romans (subject) <span class=\"strong\">created</span> the superstition about the broken mirror.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Passive sentence = The broken mirror superstition (subject) <span class=\"strong\">was created</span> by the Romans.<br/>It is not necessary to mention the object in a passive sentence. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You make the passive form of a verb by using tenses of <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> followed by the past participle. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Simple Past passive form is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "was/were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": " For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The curse  <span class=\"strong\">was lifted</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "This superstition was created by the Romans.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Damaging a mirror was viewed the same as damaging one's health.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was thought that this curse could only be corrected in the next seven year cycle.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "curse ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a difficult time caused by a bad superstition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This curse could be corrected in a seven year cycle.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about superstitions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to conquer", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to win in a war", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would conquer any country in winter if I liked the cold.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Mongolia", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a country in Asia, between Russia and China", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I would conquer Mongolia if I liked the cold.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gladiator", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a fighter in shows in ancient Rome", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If I were younger, I would fight that gladiator.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "invasion", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the entrance in an enemy territory by an army", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't make the next invasion of Germany.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "antidote ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that prevents or works against negative effects", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: With many superstitions there are some antidotes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to counter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to oppose; to block", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can counter the broken mirror superstition.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to spin", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to rotate rapidly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're supposed to spin three times.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "counterclockwise", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the opposite direction of the movement of the hands of a clock", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Spin in a counterclockwise direction.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob09aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "In pairs, write a dialogue about 12-15 sentences long.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One person has just broken a mirror and one  person is the fortune teller.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The fortune teller must explain all the bad things that can happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The fortune teller must explain what the other person is supposed to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The fortune teller must also offer a possible antidote to reverse the curse.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give advice using \"If I were you ...\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change partners.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about things I was supposed to do and things that were supposed to happen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I can talk about hypothetical situations.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about manners, customs and superstitions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I was supposed to do and                           things that were supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you know why a broken mirror is seven years bad luck?", "type": "Free Header Item"},